{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Store-aware git status (the path->store resolver, read side): runs porcelain status (-uall --no-renames, so a rename reads as its delete plus its add) through dev.git.read and translates every data/<lib>/ path into its store identity - control, facet attachment, command record, typed impl, _patches journal, controls index, asset, publish metadata (_APPS) - grouped by unit (lib.control, or the bare lib for library-level files and for records the live store no longer knows). Generated sources join their unit from <crate>/src/<lib>/<ctl>/: newbound_core for the core libraries, the library's own crate in a repositories/* clone. Deleted store paths are named via git show HEAD:. EVERY dirty path is reported exactly once with its path: store paths as items {state, what, path} under groups, everything else as {state, path} in other_paths (the text render still collapses untracked non-store noise to per-directory counts, as does `other`). A committer that commits each group's paths and other_paths with dev.git.commit_paths leaves the tree clean. Returns {groups, other, other_paths, text} - text is the render the git panel's 'store' button shows. Read-only.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"olzqvh1a05d34239fp1","readers":[],"time":1794329342586,"username":"system","writers":[]}